# A USB keyboard on the xHCI controller: found at boot, and what is typed on
# it (through QEMU, not the serial port) reaches the shell, with the layout,
# Shift and key repeat.
@usb kbd
$ layout us
$ lsusb
~ ^xHCI controller [0-9a-f]{4}:[0-9a-f]{4}, \d+ ports$
~ ^port \d+: 0627:0001 keyboard, \w+ speed \(in use, 0 reports\)$
@keys e c h o spc shift+u s b spc 1 2 3 shift+1 ret
$wait
Usb 123!
$ lsusb
~ keyboard, \w+ speed \(in use, [1-9]\d* reports\)

# Editing keys: left arrow and backspace change the line before Enter.
@keys e c h o spc a b x c left backspace ret
$wait
abc

# A key held down repeats.
@keys z:1500 ret
$wait
~ ^z{8,}: command not found

# Another layout applies to the USB keyboard too (Belgian: the q key gives a).
$ layout be
@keys e c h o spc q ret
$wait
a
